= Education policy

A school programme is large: 1 B for 4 months of building, then 1 B to run, in up to three separate tranches. The same scope of schools is never financed twice.

[+ pl_gc_budget +]

[+ pl_gc_projects +]

- @rural_access
- @urban_worker_adult_access
- @secular
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@rural_access
title: Village schools
subtitle: Schools for the villages covered; the trust of the recipients grows when the schools work (+4).
choose-if: {! return PolishProjects.optionStatus(Q, 'education_program', 'rural_access').available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_education_program_rural_access_why +]
on-arrival: {!
PolishProjects.chooseOption(Q, 'education_program', 'rural_access');
!}
go-to: result

@urban_worker_adult_access
title: Education of the poor and adults in workers’ centres
subtitle: The trust of the recipients grows (+4); it does not replace TUR.
choose-if: {! return PolishProjects.optionStatus(Q, 'education_program', 'urban_worker_adult_access').available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_education_program_urban_worker_adult_access_why +]
on-arrival: {!
PolishProjects.chooseOption(Q, 'education_program', 'urban_worker_adult_access');
!}
go-to: result

@secular
title: A secular school with religious freedom
subtitle: Needs its law; PSChD judges the content by its programme. Against an agreed religious compromise it breaks that agreement.
choose-if: {! return PolishProjects.optionStatus(Q, 'education_program', 'secular').available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_education_program_secular_why +]
on-arrival: {!
PolishProjects.chooseOption(Q, 'education_program', 'secular');
!}
go-to: result

